{"ts": 0.032618, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 2 · Paths and the filesystem\u001b[0m \u001b[90m────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 249}
{"ts": 0.034421, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSTAGE 2 — Paths and the filesystem\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFour lessons, then a gate. The shell is always \u001b[36msomewhere\u001b[0m in\r\nthe filesystem; this stage teaches you to see where, look around,\r\nmove, and predict where files land.\r\n\r\nYou'll use:\r\n  \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[0m   print where you are now\r\n  \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m    list what's in the current folder\r\n  \u001b[92mcd\u001b[0m    change to another folder\r\n\r\nAnd the path symbols:\r\n  \u001b[36m.\u001b[0m     this folder\r\n  \u001b[36m..\u001b[0m    the parent folder\r\n  \u001b[36m~\u001b[0m     your home folder\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to begin lesson 2.1.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 560}
{"ts": 0.034875, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
