{"ts": 0.143578, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m2.4 — names for places\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree short names point at places in the tree you have seen:\r\n  \u001b[36m.\u001b[0m    here, the current directory\r\n  \u001b[36m..\u001b[0m   one level up, the parent\r\n  \u001b[36m~\u001b[0m    your home folder\r\n\r\nA \u001b[36mpath\u001b[0m names a place. \u001b[36mRelative\u001b[0m paths start where you are:\r\n  \u001b[90mpractice/notes.txt\u001b[0m   a file inside a subfolder\r\n  \u001b[90m../notes.txt\u001b[0m         a file in the parent folder\r\n\u001b[36mAbsolute\u001b[0m paths start from the root, \u001b[95m/\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[90m/etc/hosts\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[90m/usr/bin/vim\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[91mPredict before you act.\u001b[0m  In \u001b[90m~/projects\u001b[0m, \u001b[92mcat notes.txt\u001b[0m\r\nreads \u001b[90m~/projects/notes.txt\u001b[0m. For another folder, name it.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to take Stage 2's gate.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 738}
